g herself a  disservice and making her acid reflux  worse if she were my client i would  definitely want to experiment with  having more  energy dense meals and snacks to see if  having  more food on board would actually help  to reduce  her symptoms so now let's get to the  stats  and again the trigger warning that i am  going to be talking about numbers so  feel free to skip ahead  to the timestamp on screen so after  crunching  the numbers on average marla is  consuming around 850 calories a day  which goes up slightly to around 1200  calories on  days when she goes out to eat with her  friends she's also consuming a pretty  low carb diet with around  42 of her calories from carbs 16  from protein and 41 from fat now with  that said  her caloric intake is definitely very  low  for someone marla's age especially  considering that she  is still you know in her young adulthood  years  and requires more calories to support  growth and development  typically the average active girl around  her age  would require around 2000 to 2400  calories a day  which is actually more than what the  average adult woman needs  so this means that based on what we are  seeing here  in this week marla is getting less than  half of her energy needs  and that's a serious issue also because  she's just generally not eating enough  food  she's also critically low on a bunch of  micronutrients as well  particularly those that are important  for teens and young adults for growth so  things like  calcium vitamin d potassium zinc and  iron now before we talk  further about this let's discuss what i  like about marla's diet first of all i  like that marla has some  good variety in her meals and aside from  not eating dairy  she doesn't appear to eliminate any  major food groups or  types of foods some days she'll eat a  salad for lunch  while others she's gonna open the  burgers and fries  so it's really great to see this type of  flexibility in her food choices  and that she isn't purposefully